{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lv7eTiVsE4YnXqDuTmA3aN","type":"tool_result","content":"Usage: klar [options] [command]\n\nklar — color accessibility tools (OKCA contrast algorithm) for AI coding agents\nand the terminal\n\nOptions:\n  -v, --version                                  output the version number\n  --no-plugins                                   Disable discovery of contrast-algorithm plugins (security: run core only)\n  -h, --help                                     display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  contrast [options] <foreground> <background>   Calculate contrast between a foreground and a background. OKCA is polarity-aware — argument order matters (some plugins are too).\n  pair [options]                                 Generate a random accessible color pair\n  variants [options] <color>                     Generate a grid of color variants (adaptive deltaE spacing by default)\n  meta [options] <color>                         Get OKLCH metadata for a color\n  match [options] <color1> <color2>              Match chroma values between two colors\n  lightness [options] <color>                    Get min/max lightness range for a color in sRGB gamut\n  find [options] <base-color> <reference-color>  Find a color that meets a target contrast by adjusting lightness\n  plugins                                        List registered contrast algorithm plugins\n  help [command]                                 display help for command\n#B3261E\n{\n  \"contrast\": 5,\n  \"type\": \"okca\",\n  \"colorOne\": \"#B3261E\",\n  \"colorTwo\": \"#FFFFFF\",\n  \"gamut\": {\n    \"map\": \"css\",\n    \"outOfGamut\": false\n  }\n}\n#0B5FBF\n{\n  \"contrast\": 5.1,\n  \"type\": \"okca\",\n  \"colorOne\": \"#0B5FBF\",\n  \"colorTwo\": \"#FFFFFF\",\n  \"gamut\": {\n    \"map\": \"css\",\n    \"outOfGamut\": false\n  }\n}\n#1B7A2E\n{\n  \"contrast\": 4.8,\n  \"type\": \"okca\",\n  \"colorOne\": \"#1B7A2E\",\n  \"colorTwo\": \"#FFFFFF\",\n  \"gamut\": {\n    \"map\": \"css\",\n    \"outOfGamut\": false\n  }\n}\n#8A4B00\n{\n  \"contrast\": 5.6,\n  \"type\": \"okca\",\n  \"colorOne\": \"#8A4B00\",\n  \"colorTwo\": \"#FFFFFF\",\n  \"gamut\": {\n    \"map\": \"css\",\n    \"outOfGamut\": false\n  }\n}\n#7B3FA0\n{\n  \"contrast\": 5.4,\n  \"type\": \"okca\",\n  \"colorOne\": \"#7B3FA0\",\n  \"colorTwo\": \"#FFFFFF\",\n  \"gamut\": {\n    \"map\": \"css\",\n    \"outOfGamut\": false\n  }\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da0086de-3b20-57a1-97ca-069a78e742e3","uuid":"d0dd096f-8f15-433b-be8b-ed044578901c","timestamp":"2026-09-29T10:35:43.219Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Usage: klar [options] [command]\n\nklar — color accessibility tools (OKCA contrast algorithm) for AI coding agents\nand the terminal\n\nOptions:\n  -v, --version                                  output the version number\n  --no-plugins                                   Disable discovery of contrast-algorithm plugins (security: run core only)\n  -h, --help                                     display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  contrast [options] <foreground> <background>   Calculate contrast between a foreground and a background. OKCA is polarity-aware — argument order matters (some plugins are too).\n  pair [options]                                 Generate a random accessible color pair\n  variants [options] <color>                     Generate a grid of color variants (adaptive deltaE spacing by default)\n  meta [options] <color>                         Get OKLCH metadata for a color\n  match [options] <color1> <color2>              Match chroma values between two colors\n  lightness [options] <color>                    Get min/max lightness range for a color in sRGB gamut\n  find [options] <base-color> <reference-color>  Find a color that meets a target contrast by adjusting lightness\n  plugins                                        List registered contrast algorithm plugins\n  help [command